outdoors each day is currently the only myopia‑prevention method backed by randomized trials"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"No screen time for children aged 0–3; limit it as much as possible for ages 3–6; for school‑age kids, non‑educational screen use should not exceed one hour per day"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Treating myopia as a lasting injury: the higher the prescription, the greater the future risk of retinal detachment, macular degeneration, and glaucoma"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Take a close look at your child’s annual school health report and follow up on any abnormalities right away"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Conducting a depression screening for kids aged 12 to 18 — don’t rely on school mental health assessments as a diagnosis"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Do not buy products or services claiming to “cure myopia” or “reduce refractive error”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Clear rules exist for sleep, homework, sports, and rankings; if schools fail to comply, parents can raise the issue"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/30-11","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Parents can request a temporary leave of absence for their child; the school must retain the child’s enrollment status for up to one year"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"If poor vision is detected, go to the hospital for cycloplegic refraction and follow up at the recommended intervals as advised by the doctor"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Pit and fissure sealants applied after permanent molars emerge"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"If your child loves playing games, first check if sleep, homework, and outdoor activities have been displaced, rather than just focusing on how long they have played"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"When a child says they are attracted to the same sex: Do not scold, do not kick them out, and do not send them to \"conversion therapy\": The attitude at home is related to whether they will attempt suicide"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Do not hit your child, and do not yell or call them stupid: children who are often hit or verbally abused show more behavior and emotional problems"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"If parenting feels out of control and you keep hitting or yelling, take a class that teaches concrete parenting skills"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/30-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"Do not send children to closed “internet addiction schools” or “special training camps”: harmful methods are prohibited by law, and children have died in confinement"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/30"},"children":["Chapter 30"," ·"," ","Children after starting school"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"30-11"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["11"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-b"},"children":["Evidence"," ","B"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Parents can request a temporary leave of absence for their child; the school must retain the child’s enrollment status for up to one year"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["A temporary leave of absence is a fully established procedure. Parents or legal guardians submit a request, which the school then approves and forwards to the relevant education authorities for final authorization. Each request is valid for no more than one year; if the child still needs time off after that, a new request must be filed. During this period, the school is legally required to keep the child’s enrollment status intact. Therefore, the idea that taking a leave of absence “ruins” a child’s education has no basis in current policy. Exact implementation details vary by province; parents should contact the school’s academic affairs office or local education bureau for specifics."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost involved. Parents or other legal guardians must su…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Article 16 of the “Administrative Measures for Student Enrollment Records of Primary and Secondary School Stud…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Parents can request a temporary leave of absence for their child; the school must retain the child’s enrollment status for up to one year"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hid